---
// The Frontend skill's showcase: a 6-step engineering pipeline, framed the
// way QA is — the coding agent is the junior who implements, the
// orchestrator is the senior who reviews. Not Cloud/DevOps's
// AI-compares-trade-offs framing: the closing line here is a concrete
// catch (a screenshot finding a bug the test suite missed), the same
// device QA's own diagram already uses.
//
// Box text stays plain-English, same rule as every diagram since Cloud's
// revision — technical specifics (scene-free classes, seeded collapse,
// parallax scroll) live one layer down in `details[].body`.
//
// Coordinates reused verbatim from AiWorkflowDiagram.astro: a linear 6-step
// pipeline, so the same 3x2 snake geometry (246-wide boxes, viewBox
// 820x400) applies without modification.
// Source facts: src/content/cards/frontend.md, docs/context/ui.md,
// docs/context/decisions.md, docs/context/testing.md,
// docs/context/coding-conventions.md.
---

<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 400"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="frontend-pipeline-title frontend-pipeline-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="frontend-pipeline-title">Six steps from a rendering rule to an admitted blind spot</title>
      <desc id="frontend-pipeline-desc">
        Six steps, in order. One: the client's whole job is to render
        whatever the server says is true and send player actions — it
        never calculates a final gameplay outcome itself. Two: what used
        to be one very large file is now a slim conductor delegating to
        small, focused pieces, each owning its own on-screen elements and
        state. Three: the piece that draws the tower only draws what the
        server already decided, including a collapse that's seeded
        identically so every player's screen shows the same outcome. Four:
        bricks stay a fixed size and the camera scrolls instead, since
        resizing every brick every frame would be real, repeated work for
        no visual benefit. Five: the riskiest placement math is pulled out
        into a plain class with no scene dependency, so nineteen tests can
        check it in seconds without opening the game. Six: passing every
        test still isn't the same as looking right — a bug that broke the
        on-screen drag preview passed every test and was only caught by
        rendering the actual screen and looking at it, which is now a
        stated, required step of its own.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="frontend-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="objectives" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 1, the screen never decides — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="64">1 · The screen never decides</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="82">it only shows what the</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="98">server already decided</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M261,82 L287,82" marker-end="url(#frontend-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="architecture" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 2, small pieces one conductor — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="64">2 · Small pieces, not one file</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="82">each piece owns one job</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="98">nothing grows back into one file</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M533,82 L559,82" marker-end="url(#frontend-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="implementation" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 3, the tower draws what happened — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="40" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="64">3 · Drawing, not deciding</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="82">not what it thinks happened</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="98">the same on every screen</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M682,124 L682,230" marker-end="url(#frontend-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="optimization" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4, the camera moves not the bricks — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="559" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="573" y="254">4 · The camera moves instead</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="272">bricks never resize to fit</text>
        <text class="sub" x="573" y="288">the view scrolls instead</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M559,272 L533,272" marker-end="url(#frontend-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="validation" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 5, checked without opening the game — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="287" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="301" y="254">5 · Checked without playing</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="272">in seconds, not minutes</text>
        <text class="sub" x="301" y="288">the highest-risk math first</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M287,272 L261,272" marker-end="url(#frontend-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="readiness" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 6, what the tests can't see admitted — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="230" width="246" height="84" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="254">6 · What the tests can't see</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="272">some bugs only show on screen</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="288">so the screen still gets checked</text>
      </g>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="368">The agent wrote the renderer</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="384">a screenshot, not the test suite, is what caught the bug the tests missed</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="card-diagram-caption">
    Click any step to read what it means.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
